<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;SUMMER CRUSH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Summer Crush is a romantic drama series that has gained international popularity, following the lives of young Greeks and capturing the essence of Greek culture."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOPHIA PAPADOPOULOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sophia Papadopoulos is the creator of 'Summer Crush,' an Athens-born writer-director who attributes the series' success to its authentic portrayal of Greek culture and universal themes."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARIA GEORGIOU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maria Georgiou is the lead actress of 'Summer Crush,' playing the role of Sophia, a free-spirited islander, and believes in the show's connection to Greek values and community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATHENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Athens is the birthplace of Sophia Papadopoulos and the setting for much of the show's inspiration and creation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREECE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Greece is the primary setting of 'Summer Crush' and the source of its cultural authenticity, with picturesque islands and warm hospitality contributing to its appeal."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREEK NATIONAL BROADCASTING COUNCIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Greek National Broadcasting Council provides ratings and data for 'Summer Crush,' indicating its success as the highest-rated Greek television series."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNITED STATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The United States is one of the countries where 'Summer Crush' has been broadcast, highlighting its international reach."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EUROPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Europe is another region where 'Summer Crush' has gained popularity, further emphasizing its global appeal."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Asia is also a market where 'Summer Crush' has been successful, showcasing its broad international audience."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH RIVIERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The French Riviera serves as a backdrop for the show's French-inspired episodes, evoking sun-kissed beaches and picturesque villages."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JEAN-LUC GODARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jean-Luc Godard is a French filmmaker whose work is referenced in the show's cinematography, paying homage to French New Wave traditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRANÇOIS TRUFFAUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"François Truffaut is another French filmmaker whose work is referenced in the show's cinematography, contributing to its French aesthetic."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIMONE DE BEAUVOIR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Simone de Beauvoir is a French philosopher and writer whose themes of existential crises and romantic entanglements are reflected in the show's character development."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JEAN-PAUL SARTRE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jean-Paul Sartre is a French philosopher whose works explore similar themes to those in 'Summer Crush,' contributing to its intellectual depth."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOENIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phoenix is a French indie band known for contributing to the French music scene and adding authenticity to the show's soundtrack."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phoenix is a French pop band featured in the show's soundtrack, adding to its French cultural authenticity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M is a French artist whose inclusion in the show's soundtrack enhances its French authenticity."&lt;SEP&gt;"M is a French indie musician included in the show's soundtrack, enhancing its musical authenticity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRISTINE AND THE QUEENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Christine and the Queens is a French artist featured in the show's soundtrack, contributing to its French musical identity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Christine and the Queens is a French artist recognized for her contributions to the French music scene and the show's soundtrack."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOPHIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHARACTER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sophia is the character played by Maria Georgiou in 'Summer Crush,' embodying the free-spirited islander and reflecting Greek values."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FREE-SPIRITED ISLANDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHARACTER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Free-Spirited Islander is the character type played by Maria Georgiou, representing the carefree charm of Greek culture."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXISTENTIAL CRISES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Existential Crises are explored in the show's themes, reflecting the philosophical depth of the series."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROMANTIC ENTANGLEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Romantic Entanglements are a key theme in the show, drawing from French literary and philosophical traditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUN-KISSED BEACHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sun-Kissed Beaches are a visual element of the show's French-inspired episodes, evoking the French Riviera."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRYSTAL-CLEAR WATERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crystal-Clear Waters are a visual element of the show's French-inspired episodes, enhancing the scenic beauty."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH MUSIC SCENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The French music scene refers to the cultural context and network of artists and musicians based in France, providing authenticity to the show's soundtrack."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHOW'S SOUNDTRACK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The show's soundtrack is a component of the show that features music from various French artists, enhancing its cultural authenticity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHOW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The show is the primary subject, incorporating elements such as its soundtrack and cultural themes to create a French experience."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH POP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"French pop refers to the genre of popular music originating from France, contributing to the show's authentic sound."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIE MUSIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indie music refers to independent music, often characterized by a DIY ethos, contributing to the show's authentic sound."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUSH INSTRUMENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lush instrumentation refers to the rich and full-sounding musical arrangements used in the show's score, enhancing its romantic and sensual qualities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WISTFUL MELODIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wistful melodies refer to the melancholic and reflective musical themes used in the show's score, evoking romanticism and sensuality."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROMANTICISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Romanticism refers to the artistic and cultural movement emphasizing emotion and individualism, which is reflected in the show's score."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENSUALITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sensuality refers to the quality of being sexually attractive or appealing, which is highlighted in the show's score."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"French culture refers to the cultural aspects of France, including its music and art, which are represented in the show's soundtrack."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUTHENTICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Authenticity refers to the genuine and true-to-life representation of French culture in the show's soundtrack."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0347</data>
    </node>
